# SportMatch hard constraints

SportMatch is a clickable university UX prototype, not a production app. Keep it faithful, simple, predictable, and fast. Do not add features that are not in the product specification.

1. Technology: React 18 + TypeScript + Vite, Tailwind CSS, `react-router-dom` (HashRouter), `lucide-react` for icons. No backend. Persist state in `localStorage` (wrapped in try/catch). Provide a "Reset demo data" action.
2. Mobile first: design for a 390 x 844 px viewport. On desktop, render the app inside a centred phone frame (about 390 px wide, rounded corners, subtle shadow, light grey page background). Never require horizontal scrolling.
3. English UI text only, using exactly the vocabulary below.
4. Max. 50% icons: most navigation and actions must be text labels. Icons only for sports, map pin, clock/bell, and the back arrow, and always paired with a text label where possible. A star on My Player Card and a tick on JOINED are part of the specified screens.
5. No heavy maps: the meeting point is a court name plus a small static pin preview box (no map SDK, no network) and a text link "Open in Maps" that opens a Google Maps search URL in a new tab.
6. Creating a session takes at most 3 steps. Joining takes one tap. No loading spinners longer than 300 ms.
7. No chat threads or message feeds on the home screen. Chat exists only inside a session, and only for the Host and confirmed players.
8. Everything must work offline after the first load. No external requests except Google Fonts (optional, with a system-font fallback).
9. Keep the code clean: small components, typed data, no unused dependencies, a short README with run instructions.
10. Scope is young adults only (18 to 30). Do not build child profiles, parent approval, elderly modes, voice search, gentle-pace tiers, real login, real database, push notifications, GPS routes, verified skill badges, interactive maps, payment, gym-partner matching, or running and cycling pace filters.

# Vocabulary

Use these labels exactly: Session, Sport, Level (Beg., Int., Adv.), Pace / Intensity, Host, Spots, Confirmed players, Live counter, Join, Join Game, Leave Session, Lineup Sheet, Noticeboard feed, My Games, My Player Card, Attendance, No-show, Near Me, Meeting point, 1h reminder!, Are you going? (Yes / No), Session Chat.

Never use: fixtures, league, tournament, contract, chat threads, lobby.
